WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
A dot sits on a straight
track, at a marked start.

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.110
A screen drops over the track.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.180
Behind it, the dot goes back and forth.

4
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.660
The screen lifts.

5
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.360
The dot has stopped, a little
to the right of the start.

6
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.090
How far did it travel?

7
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.160
How far is it from the start?

8
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.020
Is distance the same as displacement?

9
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.210
In this mission, you'll treat velocity
as the derivative of displacement,

10
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.210
with a sign for direction.

11
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.500
You'll find acceleration as
the derivative of velocity,

12
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.020
and see when a particle is at rest.

13
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.680
And you'll integrate to
go back the other way,

14
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.650
using a starting value
to find the constant.

15
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: decide whether
distance is the same as displacement.
